{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Portions</b> — in the sense of portions, as in: <b>portions</b> [for Joseph]." "<b>And in pleasant places</b> — an adjective, as in: <b>the beloved and the pleasant</b>, and it lacks [the noun for] places, and it is figurative. Rabbi Moses said: for it is also like 'my portion.' And I will yet explain my view regarding the phrase 'my strength and my praise, YHWH.' And what seems correct to me: that it is construct to the name [YHWH], in the manner of 'my mixing-bowls of wine.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The two scriptural phrases he cites, 'the beloved and the pleasant' (2 Samuel 1:23) and 'my mixing-bowls of wine' (Song of Songs 7:3), are given in translation only since no Hebrew forms are quoted in the source; 'my strength and my praise, YHWH' likewise renders the phrase he references (Exodus 15:2)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:22.470626216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}